        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 135.96,
          "end": 138.36,
          "en": "Might be you have tables which are related, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 138.36,
          "end": 141.78,
          "en": "So we call them a parent table or child table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "or a primary key or a foreign key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 145.53,
          "en": "So we connect them with primary key, foreign key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 145.53,
          "end": 148.02,
          "en": "Complex concepts, but important to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 148.02,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "On the other hand, we have a NoSQL world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 154.02,
          "en": "where you don't actually store data in a table structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
